# Go Conventions

## Build

- Always use build tag `containers_image_openpgp` to avoid gpgme C dependency
- `CGO_ENABLED=0` for cross-compilation (except when using sqlite3 which requires CGO)
- Binaries go in `cmd/<name>/main.go`, all library code in `internal/`

## Package Structure

All packages under `internal/` — no `pkg/` directory. Key packages:
- `catalog/` — FBC rendering and channel resolution
- `imageinspect/` — OCI image label extraction
- `bundlecsv/` — ClusterServiceVersion parsing from bundle layers
- `rag/` — RAG engine, vector store, embeddings
- `rag/mcp/` — MCP server wrapping RAG engine
- `rag/ingest/` — data ingestion pipeline
- `datasource/` — `ClusterDataSource` interface (must-gather + live cluster)
- `healthcheck/` — 33 health dimension checks
- `analysis/` — central 12-step analysis orchestrator
- `adhd/` — divergent analysis engine (parallel cognitive frames)
- `claudeapi/` — Anthropic Claude API client
- `rca/` — 14-section RCA report generator

## Patterns

- Return `(result, error)` pairs; wrap errors with `fmt.Errorf("context: %w", err)`
- Constructor injection for dependencies (e.g., `rag.NewEngine(cfg)`, `adhd.NewEngine(opts)`)
- Test files alongside source: `foo_test.go` next to `foo.go`
- Use `golang.org/x/sync/errgroup` for concurrent operations
- No global state or init() functions
